=== 3. THE ARITHMETIC, RE-PRICED -- WHAT THE OCEAN LIMB WOULD HAVE TO BE ===
  27q's verdict was ARITHMETIC: land 1.26x obs and ocean 0.53x, rotated into
  phase, ADD to 1.382 against obs 1.168. Re-priced as the sharper question --
  GIVEN this vector's NH-origin and SH-land limbs, what must the SH ocean limb
  BE for the SPO total to be right, and how far is that from the observed one?

  ⚠ THE THREE LIMBS DO NOT SUM TO THE TOTAL -- the model is nonlinear and each
    limb is a zeroing DIFFERENCE. The gap is carried as a fixed REMAINDER and
    printed; every counterfactual below holds it. That is an assumption, and
    it is the size of the printed remainder.

